2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - **Why you're more correct:**
2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - - Renewables *can* technically replace fossil fuels for electricity generation—many countries already derive 50%+ of power from wind/solar/hydro
2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - - The physics works. Renewables can meet total energy demand if properly scaled and integrated
2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - - Storage technology (batteries, hydrogen, thermal storage) is improving and can address intermittency
2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - - Economic trends favor renewables—they're increasingly cheaper than fossil fuels in many markets
2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:00:06,318 - INFO - **Where your friend has a point:**
