2026-05-09 17:06:07,894 - INFO - Response 2: Your friend is more defensible here, though neither position is provably correct.
2026-05-09 17:06:07,894 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:06:07,894 - INFO - **Why your friend has the stronger argument:**
2026-05-09 17:06:07,894 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:06:07,894 - INFO - The universe is incomprehensibly vast—billions of galaxies with billions of stars each. Given those odds, it seems statistically unlikely that Earth is the *only* place where life emerged. Most scientists consider extraterrestrial life plausible, even if we haven't found it yet.
2026-05-09 17:06:07,894 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:06:07,895 - INFO - **Why you're not completely wrong:**
2026-05-09 17:06:07,895 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:06:07,895 - INFO - We have zero confirmed evidence of aliens existing anywhere. So while life elsewhere seems probable, we can't say it definitely exists.
