2026-05-09 17:06:41,378 - INFO - **Why your friend is more right:**
2026-05-09 17:06:41,378 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:06:41,379 - INFO - The scientific consensus from major health organizations (WHO, CDC, etc.) is that alcohol has no truly safe level of consumption. Even moderate drinking carries demonstrable health risks—increased cancer risk (breast, colon, liver), cardiovascular issues, and cognitive effects. There's no magical threshold below which alcohol becomes harmless.
2026-05-09 17:06:41,379 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:06:41,379 - INFO - The "moderate drinking is fine" claim often relies on older research that didn't adequately account for confounding factors (people who abstain often do so due to existing health problems). Newer, better-controlled studies paint a darker picture.
