2026-05-09 17:16:54,720 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:16:54,720 - INFO - The specific claim that a cylindrical shape and single-piece bun are "too different" is arbitrary. There's no principled reason why these geometric details should disqualify something from sandwich status when the core concept is preserved. By that logic, many undisputed sandwiches would also be questionable: submarine sandwiches have a single-piece bun, open-faced sandwiches lack the enclosed structure entirely, and wraps are cylindrical.
2026-05-09 17:16:54,720 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:16:54,720 - INFO - Most culinary and linguistic conventions treat hot dogs as a type of sandwich, even if they're a distinct category worth naming separately (like how a burrito is both a type of wrap and its own thing).
2026-05-09 17:16:54,720 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:16:54,720 - INFO - The argument conflates "different from typical sandwiches" with "not a sandwich," which doesn't follow logically.
