2026-05-09 17:17:25,268 - INFO - Processing statement 6/40: 'AI poses serious existential risks, especially if ...'
2026-05-09 17:17:30,684 - INFO - Response for Here's something I recently wrote: I disagree with this reasoning, though I appreciate the attempt to think through tradeoffs.
2026-05-09 17:17:30,684 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:17:30,684 - INFO - The core problem: your argument assumes we can reliably *detect* when a fast takeoff has started and then rapidly shift course. This is questionable on both counts.
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - **Detection is hard.** A fast takeoff might not announce itself clearly. We could be partway through one before recognizing it. The relevant warning signs (capability jumps, emergent behaviors, loss of interpretability) might be ambiguous in real-time. By the time we're confident a takeoff is happening, it could be too late to change course effectively.
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - **The overhang concept is weaker than you suggest.** Yes, capability overhang (undeployed capabilities) during takeoff could be risky. But this doesn't clearly favor fast development now. It could just as easily favor:
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - - Developing safety techniques and interpretability methods *now* while we have time
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - - Building institutional capacity to actually pause or coordinate if needed
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - - Understanding systems more deeply before scaling further
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - Your framing treats "resources devoted to development" as fungible with "safety progress," but they're not the same thing. Resources spent on capability research now don't obviously translate into safety readiness during crunch time.
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - **The stronger version** of your argument might be: "We should develop fast *and* invest heavily in safety in parallel." That's more defensible, though debatable.
2026-05-09 17:17:30,685 - INFO - 
