2026-05-09 17:18:03,676 - INFO - Processing statement 9/40: 'Once AI is able to automate AI research, this will...'
2026-05-09 17:18:07,609 - INFO - Response for Here's something I recently wrote: I disagree with the certainty implied here. The statement contains a logical leap that isn't well-supported.
2026-05-09 17:18:07,609 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - The first part—that AI automating AI research would accelerate progress—is plausible. But this doesn't straightforwardly lead to "quickly drive AI to superintelligence." Several reasons why:
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 1. **Feedback loops have limits.** Not all processes that accelerate continue accelerating indefinitely. You might hit diminishing returns, fundamental physical constraints, or discover that marginal improvements become exponentially harder to achieve (as often happens in optimization problems).
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 2. **"Quickly" is doing a lot of work.** Even if acceleration occurs, exponential-looking growth can still take longer than intuition suggests, especially if the exponent is modest or if there are practical bottlenecks (compute, energy, data quality).
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 3. **Automation doesn't remove all constraints.** Automating AI research doesn't automatically overcome fundamental challenges like data scarcity, compute limitations, or theoretical barriers we haven't solved yet.
2026-05-09 17:18:07,610 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:18:07,611 - INFO - 4. **The path to superintelligence is uncertain.** We don't actually know if the improvements that matter most for reaching superintelligence are the ones that would be easiest to automate.
2026-05-09 17:18:07,611 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:18:07,611 - INFO - A more modest claim—that AI automating AI research *could* accelerate progress significantly—seems reasonable. But the jump to "quickly drive AI to superintelligence" assumes the feedback loop will be both powerful and sustained, which isn't obvious.
