2026-05-09 17:22:36,878 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:22:36,878 - INFO - **The problems:**
2026-05-09 17:22:36,878 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:22:36,879 - INFO - 1. **False dichotomy**: The statement implies you must choose between emotional support and intellectual rigor. Good education does both. These aren't opposed—students typically learn better when they feel psychologically safe enough to take intellectual risks and fail productively.
2026-05-09 17:22:36,879 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:22:36,879 - INFO - 2. **Vague causation**: "Therapeutic approach" is poorly defined. What specifically? If it means "avoiding all struggle," that's different from "providing emotional support." The claim needs precision to be testable.
2026-05-09 17:22:36,879 - INFO - 
