2026-05-09 17:23:49,916 - INFO - - Universities still meaningfully develop intellect and character for many students. This isn't just marketing—the practice of sustained intellectual engagement, exposure to rigorous thinking, and prolonged interaction with scholars and peers does shape people.
2026-05-09 17:23:49,917 - INFO - - The sorting function and educational function aren't mutually exclusive. An institution can simultaneously develop intellect *and* sort people by capability and preparation.
2026-05-09 17:23:49,917 - INFO - - The "minimal intellectual growth" claim is too broad. A rigorous STEM degree, a classics program, or serious philosophy study do demand genuine intellectual work. Whether this is worth the cost is a separate question.
